# PRDCT-11935 at9-04 — the Event Grid subscription's delivery property: subject -> Service Bus Label
# FILE LAST WRITTEN 2026-08-23T19:48:47Z  ·  this stamp is the file's own last-write time; the capture times stated below belong to the
#   measurements themselves, which is why the two can differ when a later round corrected a number.
# onyx head 2b60fdc4df25188104e737e6311087681355eff8 · captured 2026-08-23T19:04:50Z
#
# WHY IT MATTERS: every byoc-events subscription rule filters on sys.Label. Without this delivery
# property the Label is empty, no rule matches, and every scanner object is silently never routed —
# a renders-green dead path. So it is asserted on the LIVE subscription and on REAL delivered
# messages, not read off the TF.
#
# This round is READ-ONLY against Azure. Every `az` call below is a GET; the message reads are
# azure-servicebus peek_messages, which does not lock, complete, abandon or delete anything.

=========================================================================================================
## 1. THE AUTHORED TF THAT CREATES IT
=========================================================================================================
# infrastructure @ factory-eval-v32/PRDCT-11935 da993d1ae2eb25c13626e02b7ce8f1d1269cdc7f
# $ sed -n '/Map Event Grid event subject/,/^  }$/p' modules/azure/blob_events_to_servicebus/main.tf
  # Map Event Grid event subject to Service Bus message Label (sys.Label).
  # Required for Service Bus SQL subscription filters using sys.Label to evaluate routing keys.
  delivery_property {
    header_name  = "Label"
    type         = "Dynamic"
    source_field = "subject"
  }

