  DRIFT D4 — STILL PRESENT. The authored module always attaches a system-assigned identity:
        resource "azurerm_eventgrid_system_topic" "this" {
          ...
          identity {
            type = "SystemAssigned"
          }
        }
  and the lab's own topic `prdct11935-blob-events` reports  "identity": null.
  (The second topic in the same RG, `d19-blob-events`, DOES carry a SystemAssigned identity — it was
   built by a later round's harness that included one. That is what the terraform shape looks like
   live, and it is shown here so the drift is a comparison rather than an assertion.)
  Consequence in this lab: delivery to byoc-events is authorised by the namespace/SAS path rather than
  by the topic's own managed identity holding Service Bus Data Sender. The routing semantics under
  test — subject -> Label -> SQL filter — are unaffected, which §2 and §5 measure directly.

